## mixdog-cli/src/main.rs (migrate, line ~183)
# imports: `ExtHostPool` -> `RoutedExtPool`. Build:
#    let node = ExtHostConfig { <today's literal> };
#    let native = ExtHostConfig { program: std::env::current_exe()?, args: vec!["ext-worker".into()], electron: false, ..node.clone() };
#    RoutedExtPool::new(native, node, mixdog_exthost_worker::native_methods())
# (on a current_exe error print `mixdogd migrate: ...` and return ExitCode::FAILURE like the neighbouring errors). The pool
# is used as Arc<RoutedExtPool>; `.close()` is unchanged.
# mixdog-cli is stored with bytes grep reports as binary: edit only your bytes (update-index --cacheinfo) if it is CRLF.

## Tests of other crates that build the concrete pool (mixdog-core media_wire_table.rs:337, tests/it/script_syntax.rs,
## mixdog-exthost-worker/tests/pool_e2e.rs)
# They build one ExtHostPool for themselves and keep `ExtHostPool`: nothing to change.

## Check after applying
# daemon starts; a read of a .docx and of an image is answered with no Node worker process started: `ext/status` rows
# (RoutedExtPool::status) show only ids below 65536 (Rust pool); a Node-routed method (office session) shows ids >= 65536.
